                <pb facs="0330" n="296" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg296"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Tower to Mr. Sherman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >British Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Alan Chester,
                                Mass.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1897-06-30"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 30,
                    1897</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of Mr. Day’s note, No. 713, of the 28th instant, stating that the proposal of
                    Her Majesty’s Government for a renewal of the arrangement of 1894 relative to
                    the sealing regulations in Bering Sea is not acceptable to your Government.</p>
                <p>I shall not fail to bring the contents of this note to the knowledge of Her
                    Majesty’s principal secretary of state for foreign affairs.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reginald Tower.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
